  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V2X Systems obligated $847M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. V2X Systems recorded 556 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.5M. Obligations fell 49.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $813M, while the Department of State obligated $32.5M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $1.5M. Facilities Support Services is the largest market for V2X Systems this year, accounting for $744M in obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $34.7M and Communication Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $22.1M. Historical context shows obligations ranging from $1.4B in FY21 to $2B in FY23 before the current-year decline. These figures are fiscal year to date totals for FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of V2X Systems?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the biggest buyer and obligated $813M in FY2026 to date. The Department of State obligated $32.5M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $1.5M. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $377K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets does V2X Systems serve for the federal government?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services is the largest market for V2X Systems at $744M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services and Communication Equipment Repair and Maintenance are next at $34.7M and $22.1M respectively. Other federal markets include All Other Telecommunications at $17.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $12.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
